I can see exactly what happened there.
Because the "Verification" stage was the *current* active step when the rejection happened, Material UI tried to render the TCSGLIF chip as a filled primary chip to highlight it. Depending on your theme settings, that can sometimes strip the border away and leave it looking like floating text.
Additionally, we can easily strip out that small CloseIcon cross next to the user's name so it looks much cleaner.
Here is the exact replacement block for the dynamicSteps.map return statement in **VoucherPostingStatus.js**.
Find this section (around line 965 inside the Horizontal Timeline) and replace the return ( <Step ...> ... ) block with this:
```javascript
                    return (
                      <Step key={step.state} completed={isCompleted} active={isCurrent} sx={{ opacity: viewingBatchState === "REJECTED" && index > activeStepIndex ? 0.3 : 1 }}>
                        <StepLabel StepIconComponent={() => <BigWorkflowIcon statusFlag={statusFlag} label={displayLabel} />}>
                          
                          <Chip
                            label={getRoleDisplayName(step.role)}
                            size="small"
                            // FIX 1: If it is rejected, force it to be "outlined" so it keeps the standard grey border
                            variant={isCurrent && statusFlag !== 'REJECTED' ? "filled" : "outlined"}
                            color={isCurrent && statusFlag !== 'REJECTED' ? "primary" : "default"}
                            sx={{ mt: 1, height: 22, fontSize: "0.65rem", fontWeight: "bold" }}
                          />
                          
                          {/* FIX 2: Removed the small Cross icon and "By:" prefix for a cleaner look */}
                          {(isCompleted || (isCurrent && viewingBatchState === "REJECTED")) && historyItem && (
                            <Typography 
                              variant="caption" 
                              display="block" 
                              color={statusFlag === 'REJECTED' ? "error.main" : "success.main"} 
                              sx={{ mt: 0.5, fontWeight: "bold" }}
                            >
                              {executorStr}
                            </Typography>
                          )}

                        </StepLabel>
                      </Step>
                    );

```
